        "subject": "LU-20430 tests: fix yaml.sh node.yml indentation",
        "message": "LU-20430 tests: fix yaml.sh node.yml indentation\n\nsplit_output() in lustre/tests/yaml.sh writes each node.<host>.yml\nvia an unquoted \"echo $line\". Under bash this word-splits the line\nand re-joins words with single spaces, stripping the leading\nindentation of the Build: and Node: block bodies.\n\nThe result is invalid YAML: with their fields at column 0, Build:\nand Node: parse as null, so consumers lose all build/environment\ninfo (architecture, os_distribution, version, kernel_version) and\nper-node details (architecture, mem_size, nids).\n\nThis is a regression from commit 182aa9aa01f (LU-12597), which as\npart of a \"whitespace and style cleanup\" changed echo \"$line\" to\necho $line, dropping the quotes.\n\nOnly the non-shared logdir path (do_rpc_nodes ... | split_output)\nis affected; runs with a shared logdir write each node's file\ndirectly, which is why it went unnoticed.\n\nQuote the line so indentation is preserved, and use read -r to\navoid mangling backslashes.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 182aa9aa01ff (\"LU-12597 tests: remove comma_list for MDTs part 6\")\nSigned-off-by: Robert Read <rread@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I780dd860863974113267514e6d1a7161f3b21c07\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66928\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
